---
import SiteLayout from "@layouts/SiteLayout.astro";
import ProjectLink from "@components/ProjectLink.astro";
---

<SiteLayout
  title="About"
  description="Melbourne-based developer with a Master’s in AI, writing about code, AI, and the things I'm building"
>
  <article class="page-container py-16 md:py-20">
    <p class="text-highlight text-sm font-medium">About</p>
    <h1 class="text-section mt-2 font-semibold">Arian Najafi Yamchelo</h1>

    <div class="mt-10 grid items-start gap-8 md:grid-cols-[auto_1fr] md:gap-10">
      <div
        class="size-40 shrink-0 overflow-hidden rounded-full border border-(--border) shadow-(--box-shadow) md:size-44"
      >
        <img
          src="/blog/about/arian.webp"
          alt="Arian Najafi Yamchelo"
          width="176"
          height="176"
          class="size-full origin-[28%_18%] scale-[1.85] object-cover object-[28%_18%]"
        />
      </div>
      <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
        <h2>Who I am</h2>
        <p>
          My name is Arian. I'm based in Melbourne, Australia, and I build
          things with code. I started out curious about how software works, and
          over time that curiosity turned into a deeper interest in programming,
          problem solving, and building systems that are actually useful.
        </p>

        <p>
          I have a habit of over engineering things and getting too deep into
          details until a project becomes too complicated to finish. Lately I
          have been working on changing that by focusing on shipping simple,
          imperfect things instead of waiting for a perfect version that never
          gets released.
        </p>

        <p>
          This site is where I write about what I'm learning, building, and
          thinking about.
        </p>

        <h2>What I do</h2>
        <p>
          I work across software development and AI/ML. I enjoy building
          full-stack web applications, training and deploying machine learning
          models, and exploring where those two meet. I recently finished a
          Master’s in Artificial Intelligence at Monash, and I’m based in
          Melbourne. I’m open to roles where I can keep building on both the
          product and ML side.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-section mt-14 font-semibold">Education</h2>
    <div class="mt-6 grid gap-4 sm:grid-cols-2">
      <div
        class="rounded-xl border border-(--border) bg-(--bg-elevated) p-5 shadow-(--box-shadow)"
      >
        <p class="text-highlight text-sm font-medium">Monash University</p>
        <p class="text-text-primary mt-2 font-medium">
          Master of Computer Science with Distinction
        </p>
        <p class="text-text-secondary mt-1 text-sm">Artificial Intelligence</p>
        <p class="text-text-tertiary mt-3 text-sm">Mar 2024 – May 2026</p>
      </div>
      <div
        class="rounded-xl border border-(--border) bg-(--bg-elevated) p-5 shadow-(--box-shadow)"
      >
        <p class="text-highlight text-sm font-medium">RMIT University</p>
        <p class="text-text-primary mt-2 font-medium">
          Bachelor of Information Technology with Distinction
        </p>
        <p class="text-text-secondary mt-1 text-sm">Minor in Digital Design</p>
        <p class="text-text-tertiary mt-3 text-sm">Mar 2021 – Jan 2024</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <h2 class="text-section mt-14 font-semibold">Get in touch</h2>
    <p class="text-text-secondary mt-4 max-w-xl">
      The best way to reach me is by email. Whether it's about a project, a
      question, or just to say hi — I'm happy to hear from you.
    </p>
    <ProjectLink email="hi@arii.dev" emailLabel="hi@arii.dev" />
  </article>
</SiteLayout>
